{#
  The WebUI login for the qbittorrent-prefs-check CronJob, read as QBT_CREDENTIALS through
  secretKeyRef: the username on the first line, the password on the second.
  files/prefs_check.py splits it into the QBT_USERNAME and QBT_PASSWORD apply_prefs.py reads.

  One value holding both, never a key each. A key whose whole value is one secret is a
  standalone placeholder under Flux, which would add qbittorrent_username and
  qbittorrent_password to qbittorrent's row in k8s/manifests' standalone_secret_keys.json. Any
  change to that k8s/manifests file makes the tick's narrowed apply of this containers_list
  edit refuse as most of the fleet, as configarr found at H2.5b. Two lines never collide: the
  WebUI's login form takes neither field across a line break.

  Its own Secret, not a key of qbittorrent-mullvad: the Deployment projects that one into the
  wireguard sidecar's /mullvad, so a key added there would land there as a file.
#}
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: qbittorrent-prefs-check
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
type: Opaque
stringData:
  credentials: |-
    {{ qbittorrent_username }}
    {{ qbittorrent_password }}
